---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { isPreview } from '../../lib/deployment';
---

<SiteLayout title="Info" section="About Alkemist" preview={isPreview}>
  <article class="alk-prose">
    <h1>A home for people who make things.</h1>
    <p class="alk-lead">
      Alkemist is an Astro publishing toolkit for inventors, researchers, and
      the teams around them.
    </p>
    <p>
      A useful research website can hold the explanation and the experiment
      together: a model you can turn, a chart you can inspect, and the source
      behind both. Alkemist brings those pieces into a shared language for
      publishing.
    </p>
    <h2>Built in the open</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses the same Alkemist packages it documents. The blog
      records design decisions and progress; the labs put ideas into your hands;
      the docs explain how to use the components in your own project.
    </p>
    <h2>The project</h2>
    <p>
      Alkemist lives in the <a href="https://github.com/alkemdev/alkemist"
        >alkemdev organization on GitHub</a
      >. Its source, changes, and development history are available there.
    </p>
    <h2>Make it your own</h2>
    <p>
      Use Alkemist for a personal research site, a team, a company, or an
      independent project. Your content and identity belong to your site; shared
      components and defaults live in packages that can evolve.
    </p>
    <div class="alk-links">
      <a href="/blog/">Follow the work →</a><a href="/docs/">Read the docs →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
